  "notes": [
    "Run with scripts/parity/capture_driver.py against the frozen canonical macOS app (unix socket) and the Windows Tauri backend (named pipe).",
    "UUIDs are symbolized by creation order by the driver; refs (workspace:N/surface:N) are compared verbatim.",
    "approved_differences carry JSON pointers into the case observation and are consumed by scripts/parity/differential_harness.py; only genuinely platform-scoped values (live terminal titles embedding the shell name, native default-shell text per the contract's platform_equivalence clause) are approved.",
    "session_setup builds the shared fixture workspace; each case owns any extra fixture it needs so cases stay order-insensitive beyond the shared fixture."
